Loom AIE2P array plans: constrain.prefix %channel, %binding, %bytes. The first |bytes| of an ingress channel's stream
come from the start of another binding: the shim chains a descriptor on that binding ahead of the channel's own (one
more shim descriptor; the main transfer is the channel's records minus the prefix's). A host can then rebind a small
per-call prefix (the NPU attention's query payloads) while every call streams the same large binding after it (the
K / V records of one KV head). The channel must own its shim channel, carry whole records in the prefix, and transfer
once (no task repeat, chain, iteration, or panel). Programs without the op emit byte-identical.

